# Root-level environment variables.
#
# ITUN has an account-gated backend (Convex) as of ADR-030/ADR-034 — the
# "local-first, no auth/backend" description that used to sit here described
# ADR-001, which ADR-030 superseded. It still RUNS with none of these set: an
# unset VITE_CONVEX_URL means the account gate is off and storage is local.
#
# Per-app env (e.g. the Discord bot's DISCORD_TOKEN) lives in each app's own
# .env / .env.example. None of the VITE_-prefixed variables below is a secret —
# anything VITE_-prefixed is inlined into the browser bundle, so never put one
# there that is.

# --- apps/itun ---
# Convex deployment URL. Unset = no backend: nobody can sign in, so everything
# built is in-memory only and lost on reload (ADR-034). There is no longer a
# flag that makes anonymous work durable — the `local` backend was retired.
VITE_CONVEX_URL=
# Test-only auth bridge, and the observability self-probe.
VITE_TEST_AUTH=
VITE_OBSERVABILITY_PROBE=

# --- both browser apps ---
# Sentry. With no DSN the SDK is tree-shaken out and the build looks identical
# to a working one — see tools/check-observability.ts.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# Commit SHA, used as the Sentry release.
VITE_COMMIT_REF=
